  =========================Loops=======================================

  performing Repetitive tasks

  - while loop

    variable;
    while(condition on variable)
    {
      this code will execute till the time condition is true;
      I/D;
    }

  - for loop


      for(variable;condition on variable;I/D)
      {
        this code will execute till the time condition is true;
      }

  - advanced for loop

//Usages of while & for loop
  // number of iterations are not fixed --- while loop
  // number of iterations are fixed     --- for loop

// To store group of values of similar data types ===> Arrays
// To perform operation over group of vales ==>while loop, for loop, advanced for loop, display ->Arrays.toString(arrayName);

Day 23:
Define Class:  A class is a Template
Define Object: Every copy of the Template is known as its Object
relationship b/w class and Object: A class is a Template and every copy of the class is called its object
Technically: NameOfTheCLassWhoseCopyYouWantToCreate nameOfCopy = new NameOfTheClassWhoseCopyYouWantToCreate();
Object w.r.t main();//Object(copy) should be created within the main();
Visual Representation of Class and Object
different object scenarios
Garbage collector
Object to object assignment

NameOfTheCLassWhoseCopyYouWantToCreate nameOfCopy = new NameOfTheClassWhoseCopyYouWantToCreate();

Larry

Larry lar1 = new Larry();

